5dt01045d","Year":2025,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-027399","value":"30.9 ± 0.6","numeric":30.9}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"value":1.67,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1021/jm4001665","year":2013,"counterion":"[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-000981","detection":"Fluorescence","method_description":"The lipophilicity (log Po/w) was measured according to the literature method. Equal amounts of n-octanol and phosphate-buffered saline (PBS) were thoroughly mixed in the oscillator for 24 hours. The mixture was then left to separate for a further 24 hours in order to obtain water and oil phase both which were saturated with the other. 1-3 were carefully dissolved in PBS (saturated with n-octanol) and obtained the saturated solution at room temperature (concentration denoted as Co). The saturated solution was then mixed with an equal amount of n-octanol (saturated with PBS) and shaken on oscillator for another 24 hours. After separation, the final concentration of1-3 in water phase as denoted as Cw. Both Co and Cw were measured by emission spectra area between 380-700 nm at the excitation light lex=350 nm. The lipophilicity of 1-3 was calculated according to the equation: log Po/w= log [(Co- Cw)/Cw]."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir-2","value":0.21,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2022.112050","year":2023,"counterion":"[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-003864","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The log POW values of Ir-1~Ir-4 were determined by using the classical shake-flask method. Briefly, excess Ir-1~Ir-4 were dispersed in double-distilled water presaturated with n-octanol. Then the same volume of n-octanol (presaturated with water) was added, and shaken vigorously for 2 h. The concentrations of compounds in an aqueous phase were calculated by the UV-vis spectrum method, and the log POW value were then determined."}]}